# Patch for CVE-2026-31802
# Fix symlink path traversal via drive-relative linkpath in node-tar
#
# When a symlink entry has a linkpath like C:../../../etc/passwd, the path
# traversal check resolves it using path.posix.join(entryDir, p) where p is
# the raw linkpath string (still containing the drive-letter prefix after
# root-stripping happens later). This allows the resolved path to escape the
# extraction directory on Windows-style drive-relative paths.
#
# Fix: use path.posix.join(entryDir, parts.join('/')) instead of p so that
# the already-sanitized parts array (with root stripped and backslashes
# normalized) is used for resolution, preventing the escape.
#
# Note: applies AFTER CVE-2026-29786 (alphabetical order), so 'parts' is
# already the root-stripped, backslash-normalized version of the linkpath.
